{"timestamp":"2026-10-19T09:15:43.156Z","level":"info","event":"provider.together.response","fields":{"provider":"together","endpoint":"/chat/completions","response":{"httpStatus":200,"contentType":"text/event-stream","providerRequestId":"71aa12ee-aws_ec1","model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K3","text":"\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"outline-v1\",\n  \"targetDurationSeconds\": 180,\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"hook\",\n      \"title\": \"Gift or Harvest? Changing the Conversation on Righteousness\",\n      \"description\": \"Frame the lesson focus: many believers know righteousness only as God's gift, but there is also a righteousness seen as a harvest of what is done. Pose the question—what are the different manifestations of righteousness, and how do they apply to the Christian believer?\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a15370-64c3-7be2-82c0-e526abb056b5\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"92b36f9c-4010-7482-97b9-74dba2360041\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 20\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Two Manifestations: Gift and Harvest\",\n      \"description\": \"Teach the core distinction: righteousness received as God's gift to all who believe, versus righteousness produced as a harvest on account of obedience. Emphasize that the harvest is not a prerequisite to the believer's relationship with God but its indistinguishable fruit.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a15370-64c3-7be2-82c0-e526abb056b5\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"a4e0b144-3c02-733c-a1f1-8de6f04f39a7\", \"4c445771-18b7-79e6-9638-a5b3f299781d\", \"37fa72b9-ef28-72ab-ae23-f64cc0daa641\", \"20e6ced3-4382-7adf-915e-1e06d95467a0\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Sowing and Reaping: 2 Corinthians 9:6–10\",\n      \"description\": \"Explain the sowing-and-reaping principle: whoever sows bountifully reaps bountifully; God loves a cheerful giver; God makes all grace abound so believers may abound in every good work; and He increases 'the harvest of your righteousness'—generosity as a practical demonstration of righteousness.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a15370-64c3-7c60-bfd2-c5d00f92e836\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"c0a8a43c-a6b9-7a41-a68a-bcb11ff45d2c\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"example\",\n      \"title\": \"Adam's Planted Garden and David's Two Presentations\",\n     ","textChunks":["\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"outline-v1\",\n  \"targetDurationSeconds\": 180,\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"hook\",\n      \"title\": \"Gift or Harvest? Changing the Conversation on Righteousness\",\n      \"description\": \"Frame the lesson focus: many believers know righteousness only as God's gift, but there is also a righteousness seen as a harvest of what is done. Pose the question—what are the different manifestations of righteousness, and how do they apply to the Christian believer?\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a15370-64c3-7be2-82c0-e526abb056b5\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"92b36f9c-4010-7482-97b9-74dba2360041\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 20\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Two Manifestations: Gift and Harvest\",\n      \"description\": \"Teach the core distinction: righteousness received as God's gift to all who believe, versus righteousness produced as a harvest on account of obedience. Emphasize that the harvest is not a prerequisite to the believer's relationship with God but its indistinguishable fruit.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a15370-64c3-7be2-82c0-e526abb056b5\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"a4e0b144-3c02-733c-a1f1-8de6f04f39a7\", \"4c445771-18b7-79e6-9638-a5b3f299781d\", \"37fa72b9-ef28-72ab-ae23-f64cc0daa641\", \"20e6ced3-4382-7adf-915e-1e06d95467a0\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Sowing and Reaping: 2 Corinthians 9:6–10\",\n      \"description\": \"Explain the sowing-and-reaping principle: whoever sows bountifully reaps bountifully; God loves a cheerful giver; God makes all grace abound so believers may abound in every good work; and He increases 'the harvest of your righteousness'—generosity as a practical demonstration of righteousness.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a15370-64c3-7c60-bfd2-c5d00f92e836\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"c0a8a43c-a6b9-7a41-a68a-bcb11ff45d2c\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"example\",\n      \"title\": \"Adam's Planted Garden and David's Two Presentations\",\n     "," \"description\": \"Compare vertical and horizontal righteousness. Adam woke to a garden planted by God: righteousness originates as a divine gift (seed) but must be planted in the soil of practical obedience to produce a crop. Vertically before God, human efforts are like filthy rags; horizontally before men, faith is seen through visible works—David spoke covenant privilege to Goliath but gave Saul a practical resume of the lion and the bear.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a15370-64c3-77a0-aab1-ac7c67c0dae7\", \"01a15370-64c3-7be2-82c0-e526abb056b5\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"e147175f-4e18-768e-8087-df130de3689b\", \"04360068-2f11-7415-a410-5834e33afc74\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 35\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"concept\",\n      \"title\": \"Tzedakah: The Three Dimensions of Righteousness\",\n      \"description\": \"Define the Hebrew term tzedakah and its three scriptural dimensions: personal morality (moral conduct, avoiding sin, purity), justice (standing up for the oppressed, illustrated by the Good Samaritan where religious leaders had ceremonial righteousness but lacked active justice), and charity/generosity (caring for the needy, illustrated by Abraham offering Isaac, where faith was perfected by works—'Now I know').\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a15370-64c3-7f64-a364-80c420688850\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"75201c02-1f3b-7394-87bf-b0b881063efb\", \"840ff55a-7674-794a-9647-bfdcbb4d1f63\", \"8ebf28eb-e65d-72d1-b81f-d44070a45818\", \"a3ea6e62-8a7f-719f-b99a-a993e3d4ddae\", \"91ec572c-9242-737d-b80e-689ef93077b9\", \"f854e275-2499-7853-92af-cea1314dce65\", \"c7ee7328-781f-7b6e-a93d-dd1bdaa2b069\", \"9c8ccd05-72d7-768b-9a4b-cd41813e3158\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 35\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"analogy\",\n      \"title\": \"Seed, Soil, and Crop: Applying the Framework to the Believer\",\n      \"description\": \"Apply the gift-versus-harvest framework to the Christian life using the seed/soil/crop picture: the believer receives the gift (seed), plants it in the soil of practical obedience, and the vi","sible works that result are the crop—the indistinguishable fruit of a relationship with God, not a prerequisite for it. Invite learners to identify where their own 'seed' needs planting.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a15370-64c3-7225-95dc-eec6df2991bf\", \"01a15370-64c3-7be2-82c0-e526abb056b5\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"e147175f-4e18-768e-8087-df130de3689b\", \"a4e0b144-3c02-733c-a1f1-8de6f04f39a7\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 20\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"summary\",\n      \"title\": \"Summary: From Gift to Harvest\",\n      \"description\": \"Recap: righteousness is both God's gift to all who believe and a harvest produced through obedience; 2 Corinthians 9 shows generosity increasing the harvest of righteousness; vertical righteousness is before God while horizontal righteousness is demonstrated before people through visible works; tzedakah spans personal morality, justice, and charity; and for the believer, works are the fruit of relationship with God, never a prerequisite.\",\n      \"objectiveIds\": [\"01a15370-64c3-7be2-82c0-e526abb056b5\", \"01a15370-64c3-7c60-bfd2-c5d00f92e836\", \"01a15370-64c3-77a0-aab1-ac7c67c0dae7\", \"01a15370-64c3-7f64-a364-80c420688850\", \"01a15370-64c3-7225-95dc-eec6df2991bf\"],\n      \"sourceBlockIds\": [\"92b36f9c-4010-7482-97b9-74dba2360041\", \"a4e0b144-3c02-733c-a1f1-8de6f04f39a7\", \"c0a8a43c-a6b9-7a41-a68a-bcb11ff45d2c\", \"04360068-2f11-7415-a410-5834e33afc74\", \"840ff55a-7674-794a-9647-bfdcbb4d1f63\"],\n      \"estimatedSeconds\": 10\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"],"textChunksTruncated":false,"textCharacters":5471,"reasoningCharacters":0,"finishReason":"stop","inputTokens":"[REDACTED]","outputTokens":"[REDACTED]"},"retries":0,"latencyMs":23430,"service":"pipeline-worker","correlationId":"01a15340-392d-7857-963f-cdd8411984c1"}}
